s and exceptions to those rules [Data: Entities (1257, 1258); Relationships (1569, 1570)].\\n\\nThis is important because it clarifies that the turnout community includes both standard and non-standard voting behavior within an official framework. The data does not indicate irregularity; it only shows that the election process accounted for voters whose ballots were cast outside their domicile-assigned station [Data: Entities (1257, 1258); Relationships (1569, 1570)].\"},{\"summary\":\"The special ballot box is explicitly represented\",\"explanation\":\"URNA SPECIALĂ is identified as the special ballot box used by a subset of voters to cast their votes. Its direct relationship to ALEGĂTORILOR indicates that some voters participated through this alternative voting mechanism [Data: Entities (1259, 1251); Relationships (1571)].\\n\\nThis adds another layer to the election administration picture, showing that the community includes accommodations for voters who did not vote through the standard ballot-box pathway. The data supports only the existence of this mechanism and its use by some voters, not any broader inference about why it was used [Data: Entities (1259); Relationships (1571)].\"},{\"summary\":\"The two finalists are the key political actors in the race\",\"explanation\":\"CEI DOI CANDIDAȚI are described as the two finalists in the presidential race, and the race is directly linked to them. This makes them the principal competitive actors in the political portion of the community [Data: Entities (1245, 1250); Relationships (1556)].\\n\\nTheir role is reinforced by the fact that they were invited to a debate and later confronted each other on television, showing that they were not only finalists but also the focal point of public political engagement around the race [Data: Entities (1245, 964); Relationships (1556, 1550)].\"},{\"summary\":\"The President of Romania is connected to the debate context\",\"explanation\":\"PREȘEDINTELE is described as the Presiden